    "q-135297": {
      "dom_id": "step-q135297",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "What surface is defined by the equation $\\rho =1$ in spherical polar coordinates?",
      "worked_solution": "We write the position of a point (vector) in spherical polar coordinates as $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ),$ where \n\n- $\\rho \\ge 0$ is the distance from the point to the origin,\n\n- $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ is the angle between the point and the positive $x$-axis, and\n\n- $ϕ\\in [0,\\pi ]$ is the angle the corresponding vector makes with the positive $z$-axis.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our equation:\n\n$$\n\\rho =1\n$$\n\nThis equation specifies that for any point on the surface, the distance from the point to the origin must equal $1.$ On the other hand, $\\theta $ and $ϕ$ can vary arbitrarily in their respective domains. \n\nTherefore, our surface is a sphere.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14220306/assets/6bca743f355735dae56d679cc601852f5a52bd5cc99e89a8d4f20a92111cf621.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-135297-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A half-cone",
              "html": "A half-cone"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-135297-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A cone",
              "html": "A cone"
            },
            {
              "option": "c",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-135297-c",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A half-plane that passes through the $z$-axis",
              "html": "A half-plane that passes through the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"124\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D467 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>-axis"
            },
            {
              "option": "d",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-135297-d",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A sphere",
              "html": "A sphere"
            },
            {
              "option": "e",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-135297-e",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A plane that is parallel to the $xy$-plane",
              "html": "A plane that is parallel to the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"125\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D466 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>-plane"
            }
          ],
